# Keep the knowledge graph a clean CODE graph.
#
# The post-commit/post-checkout hooks rebuild structurally (AST only, no LLM).
# For markdown that means disconnected heading-trees with NO edges into the code
# graph — pure node-count bloat that wrecks the "weakly-connected nodes" signal
# and clutters the visualization. So exclude docs from graph extraction.
#
# NOTE: this also applies to manual `/graphify` runs. To do a deliberate run that
# includes docs (e.g. the LLM prose->code pass), temporarily remove or comment
# these lines, then restore them.
#
# To switch to "exclude superpowers only", delete the *.md / docs/ lines below
# and keep just `docs/superpowers/`.

*.md
*.mdx
*.qmd
docs/

# Non-app code excluded from the graph: research notes, the LegiScan API
# reference, and CI/workflow config aren't part of the application architecture.
research/
legiscan/
.github/
